  "reason": "The exact 256x128 opaque-diamond alpha contract passes with 16,384 fully opaque interior pixels, 16,384 fully transparent exterior pixels, no partial alpha, and zero exterior/chroma residue. The image uses a broad pale worn-limestone field across the left-center, two irregular cool-gray mineral peninsulas, and one restrained warm calcite/mineral accent fan; these remain low-frequency, non-repeating, prop-free at the rim, and readable beneath units and route overlays. Its pale limestone/calcite/mineral palette, upper-left modeling, and crisp cave material treatment fit the cave reference without copying its composition. No grid, path-like stripe, repeated stamp, forest material, text, framing, detached fragment, or visible generation defect is present.",
